//     IPv6 (ULA) prefixes from /48 through /64. A private entry may
//     state `cidr` instead of `family` + `size` (see
//     `InitialPrefixRequest`); i3D.net selects the subnet for every
//     entry without one. They take `addressing.prefixes[]` when given,
//     otherwise exactly one IPv4 /24 is allocated in your private
//     address space. Other private masks are rejected with a `422`.
//   - `addressing.source: none` provisions zero prefixes.
